Connect to a MongoDB® Database Instance using locally installed mongosh.

When no username is given, the first db_admin user is used (falling back to the first user). With the default template, mongosh prompts for the password unless password= is provided (in which case it is placed in ConnURL). The instance TLS certificate is downloaded to a unique temporary file (removed when the command exits).

Use template to connect with a different tool instead. Its value (default: the mongosh command below) is rendered as a Go text/template and the result is executed as the connect command.
Available variables:
{{.InstanceID}}, {{.Instance}} (the instance object), {{.Endpoint}} ({{.Endpoint.DNSRecord}}), {{.Region}}, {{.Username}}, {{.Password}}, {{.ConnURL}}, {{.CertPath}}, {{.Organization}} and {{.Project}}.

USAGE:
  scw mongodb instance connect <instance-id ...> [arg=value ...]

EXAMPLES:
  Connect to a MongoDB instance
    scw mongodb instance connect 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

  Connect via private network
    scw mongodb instance connect 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 private-network=true

  Connect with a custom command
    scw mongodb instance connect 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 template="my-mongo-tool --uri {{.ConnURL}}"

ARGS:
  [private-network=false]                                                                Connect by the private network endpoint attached.
  instance-id                                                                            UUID of the instance
  [username]                                                                             Name of the user to connect with (defaults to the first db_admin, else the first user)
  [password]                                                                             Password for ConnURL. If omitted, the default template lets mongosh prompt for it
  [template=mongosh {{.ConnURL}} --username {{.Username}} --tlsCAFile "{{.CertPath}}"]   Command line to run instead of the default mongosh one, as a Go text/template
  [region=fr-par]                                                                        Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config (fr-par)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for connect
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use
